# layerfromcurves

- Label: Layer from Curves
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 57 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/layerfromcurves.html
- Summary (EN): The Layer from Curves node renders curve geometry into a layer, with controls for width, profile and colour. It is a higher-level alternative to Rasterize Curves and gives more control over the look of the curves.
- Résumé (FR) : Rend des courbes dans une couche avec largeur, profil et couleur contrôlables, plus finement que Rasterize Curves.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and metadata", "curves: source curve geometry to render"]

- Key parameters: ["Width / Width along Curve: width in image space, optionally varied along the curve", "Profile: adjusts the profile across the curve width", "Color along Length / Color across Width: colour along the length and across the width", "UV Twist Rate: scrolls the U value along the curve for a twisted rope look", "Tile / Tile Size / Force Tilable V: replicates curves so the layer tiles, with tile size matching the aspect ratio", "Joints / Endpoints / Max Joint Scale: corner joins (Round or Sharp), end caps (Flat or Round), and spike limit on sharp corners", "Resample / Segment Length: resamples the input curves to smooth them", "Treat Polygons As: Straight, Subdivision, Interpolating or Resample by Polygon Edge"]

- Caveats: ["size_ref must be connected, since it sets the output image size", "Subdivision smooths curves without passing through the original points; Interpolating passes through them but can oscillate", "UV outputs are intended for a Texture Sample COP, and the uvscale output helps UV Transform COP filter correctly", "The page describes this node as higher level than Rasterize Curves", "Documented as available since version 21.0"]

